      "parent_id": "HN3cOIy",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\n\nKV caching is a caching technique used in web applications to reduce server load by caching frequently accessed content based on user search keywords. When a user requests a page, the server checks if the keywords are present in the cache. If they are, the page is served from the cache; if not, it is served from the main server. This reduces the number of requests the main server has to handle, improving performance and reducing latency.",
